{"name":"Brocade","hex":"#8c87c5","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"brocade","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A thick heavy fabric into which raised patterns have been woven, originally in gold and silver; more recently any cloth incorporating raised, woven patterns.","An item decorated with brocade."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To decorate fabric with raised woven patterns."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brocade"}],"entries":[{"title":"Brocade","blocks":[{"text":"Brocade is a class of richly decorative shuttle-woven fabrics, often made in coloured silks and sometimes with gold and silver threads. The name comes from Italian broccato meaning 'embossed cloth', originally past participle of the verb broccare 'to stud, set with nails', from brocco, 'small nail', from Latin broccus, 'projecting, pointed'."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Paris_-_Cath%C3%A9drale_Notre-Dame_-_Tr%C3%A9sor_de_la_cath%C3%A9drale_-_Ornements_sacerdotaux_-3.JPG/330px-Paris_-_Cath%C3%A9drale_Notre-Dame_-_Tr%C3%A9sor_de_la_cath%C3%A9drale_-_Ornements_sacerdotaux_-3.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brocade","wikidata":"Q649022"},{"title":"Brocade (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Brocade was a British-trained Thoroughbred racehorse and broodmare. Unraced as a juvenile she began her racing career in 1984 and showed high class form to win the Oak Tree Stakes and the Challenge Stakes as well as finishing second in the Prix Quincey. After struggling to recapture her best form as a four-year-old she ended her racing career with a win in the Prix de la Forêt. She was highly successful as a broodmare, producing several winners including Barathea and Gossamer."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brocade_(horse)","wikidata":"Q104853488"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Brocart_de_soie_fran%C3%A7ais.jpg/250px-Brocart_de_soie_fran%C3%A7ais.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/86/Brocart_de_soie_fran%C3%A7ais.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Brocart_de_soie_fran%C3%A7ais.jpg/250px-Brocart_de_soie_fran%C3%A7ais.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Silk brocade fabric, Lyon, France, 1760–1770.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABrocart_de_soie_fran%C3%A7ais.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/JacaltecBrocade.jpg/330px-JacaltecBrocade.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/JacaltecBrocade.jpg/330px-JacaltecBrocade.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Detail of hair-sash being brocaded on a Jakaltek Maya backstrap loom.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJacaltecBrocade.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Brocade_loom.jpg/500px-Brocade_loom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Brocade_loom.jpg/1280px-Brocade_loom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Brocade_loom.jpg/500px-Brocade_loom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Large Yunjin brocade loom, Nanjing, China, 2010","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABrocade_loom.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Giovanni_Bellini_-_Portrait_of_Giovanni_Emo_-_National_Gallery_of_Art%2C_Washington.jpg/500px-Giovanni_Bellini_-_Portrait_of_Giov